### Peticiones de ejemplo para la extensión REST Client de VS Code o el cliente HTTP de IntelliJ.
### Corre la app primero: ./mvnw spring-boot:run

@host = http://localhost:8080
@appKey = demo-key
@appToken = demo-token

### Métodos de pago que ofrece el conector
GET {{host}}/manifest

### 1. Autorizar un pago (tarjeta que siempre se aprueba)
POST {{host}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
X-VTEX-API-AppKey: {{appKey}}
X-VTEX-API-AppToken: {{appToken}}

{
  "paymentId": "PAY-001",
  "transactionId": "TX-001",
  "orderId": "v1001-01",
  "paymentMethod": "Visa",
  "value": 1299.50,
  "currency": "MXN",
  "installments": 1,
  "card": { "holder": "Cliente Prueba", "number": "4444333322221111", "csc": "123" }
}

### 2. Capturar una parte
POST {{host}}/payments/PAY-001/settlements
Content-Type: application/json
X-VTEX-API-AppKey: {{appKey}}
X-VTEX-API-AppToken: {{appToken}}

{ "requestId": "settle-1", "value": 1000.00 }

### 3. Reembolsar
POST {{host}}/payments/PAY-001/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
X-VTEX-API-AppKey: {{appKey}}
X-VTEX-API-AppToken: {{appToken}}

{ "requestId": "refund-1", "value": 200.00 }

### 4. Pago asíncrono: responde "undefined" y avisa al callbackUrl unos segundos después.
### Cambia el callbackUrl por una URL tuya de https://webhook.site para ver llegar el aviso.
POST {{host}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
X-VTEX-API-AppKey: {{appKey}}
X-VTEX-API-AppToken: {{appToken}}

{
  "paymentId": "PAY-002",
  "transactionId": "TX-002",
  "paymentMethod": "Mastercard",
  "value": 850.00,
  "currency": "MXN",
  "card": { "number": "4222222222222224" },
  "callbackUrl": "https://webhook.site/tu-id"
}

### 5. Cancelar (solo funciona si no se ha capturado nada)
POST {{host}}/payments/PAY-002/cancellations
Content-Type: application/json
X-VTEX-API-AppKey: {{appKey}}
X-VTEX-API-AppToken: {{appToken}}

{ "requestId": "cancel-1" }
